**Occupational structure** means how workers are spread across occupations. Traders and manufacturers mark the change from village to town, but they do not depend wholly on village resources.

@up UP link: UP has India's **largest rural population** and the **second-largest urban population** (4.45 crore), but its urbanization level is only **22.3%** (2011). Its urban growth was fastest in **1971-81**.

@trap
**India urban 31.16% (2011), 27.8% (2001).** **Census town = 5,000+, 75% male non-farm workers, 400/sq km.** **3,894 census towns.** **Moderate phase 1931-61; fastest urban growth 1971-81.** **Jains most urban.** **Goa most urbanized, Himachal least; Tamil Nadu most urbanized big state.** **Maharashtra largest urban population, UP second.** **Delhi most urbanized UT; Andaman least.** **UP largest rural population.**
@end

